Spec: SpecDD Completion

Platform: IntelliJ Platform / Kotlin

Purpose:
  Provide section, file path, and local symbol completion for SpecDD files.

Structure:
  ./SpecDDSectionCompletion.kt: Section completion decision model and lookup element creation.
  ./SpecDDInlineCompletion.kt: Inline file path and local symbol completion decision model.
  ./SpecDDCompletionContributor.kt: IntelliJ completion contributor entry point.

Owns:
  ./completion.sdd
  ./SpecDDSectionCompletion.sdd
  ./SpecDDInlineCompletion.sdd
  ./SpecDDCompletionContributor.sdd
  ./SpecDDSectionCompletion.kt
  ./SpecDDInlineCompletion.kt
  ./SpecDDCompletionContributor.kt

Can modify:
  ./completion.sdd
  ./SpecDDSectionCompletion.sdd
  ./SpecDDInlineCompletion.sdd
  ./SpecDDCompletionContributor.sdd
  ./SpecDDSectionCompletion.kt
  ./SpecDDInlineCompletion.kt
  ./SpecDDCompletionContributor.kt

Can read:
  /src/main/kotlin/ai/specdd/idea/parser/*
  /src/main/kotlin/ai/specdd/idea/SpecDDFileType.kt
  /src/test/kotlin/ai/specdd/idea/completion/*

Must:
  Provide basic completion for known SpecDD section labels.
  Reuse `SpecDDLanguageFacts.sectionLabels` as the section label source.
  Propose section labels only for SpecDD files.
  Propose section labels only for basic completion.
  Propose section labels on unindented top-level lines.
  Treat empty top-level lines as valid section completion positions.
  Treat partial section label text before the caret as the completion prefix.
  Support multi-word partial prefixes such as `Can m`.
  Reject completion on indented lines because section headers must start at column 0.
  Reject completion for comments, task lines, body text, scenario steps, key-value lines, and text that cannot be a section label prefix.
  Insert completed sections as header text ending with `: `.
  Provide file path completion from paths under the current project root.
  Complete `./` and `../` path prefixes relative to the current `.sdd` file directory.
  Provide local symbol completion from symbol-like tokens already present in the current SpecDD file.
  Do not require cross-language symbol indexes for the first local symbol completion implementation.
  Cover completion prefix rules and contributor behavior with Kotest BehaviorSpec tests.

Must not:
  Define section labels independently from parser language facts.
  Implement validation diagnostics.
  Define syntax highlighting colors.
  Add user-facing settings.
